S630 SC COMPLEMENT PERSPECTIVE AND UNIT-DISTANCE CARRIER SCOUT
==============================================================================

Core object:
  Anti(T) = {sigma in Sym(V): i->j in T iff sigma(j)->sigma(i) in T}.
  If T is self-complementary and tau in Anti(T), then Anti(T)=Aut(T)*tau.
  Programmatically, this is a complementing coset of the automorphism group.

Cyclotomic guardrail
--------------------
Phi3(2)=2^2+2+1=7
3*Phi3(2)=21
centered_hex(3)=3*3*(3+1)+1=37
Reading: Phi3 supplies a visible carrier scalar, not permission
to identify unit-distance edge counts with forbidden H evaluations.

