Tournament Analysis over proof lenses
-------------------------------------
Vertices are proof/carrier lenses, not tournament vertices.
Pairwise observable: which lens preserves complement-perspective data,
unit-distance side channels, and the H-gap guardrail with less collapse.
Switches/gauges: SC-perspective, unit-distance carrier, H-gap guardrail.
Ties: insertion Hamiltonian path over the majority tournament.
score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 5: 3, 7: 1} directed_3cycles=1 H=3
tie Hamiltonian path by majority score:
  score=7: anti-coset torsor
  score=5: vertex perspective orbits
  score=5: OCF H-gap guardrail
  score=5: Eisenstein Phi3 norm
  score=3: Burnside cycle types
  score=2: unit spine carrier
  score=1: tile/bulk side channel
  score=0: raw scalar 7/21

Assumption Challenge
--------------------
Alternate vertices considered: raw tournament vertices, SC classes,
anti-automorphisms, automorphism orbits, anti-cycle types, unit-distance
points, unit edges, Hamiltonian paths, shell/bulk packets, and proof
obligations.  The chosen tournament vertices are proof/carrier lenses.
Preserved predicate: complementing-perspective duality plus the H-gap
guardrail under unit-distance carrier decompositions.
Destroyed data: full embeddings, all n>=8 SC classes, exact graph6
representatives for n=21, and continuous distance inequalities.
Challenged assumption: self-complementarity gives one canonical node swap;
the intrinsic object is the anti-coset, with a map chosen only after
coordinates are fixed.

Interpretation
--------------
- The SC node-swap object is not a single permutation; it is Anti(T),
  a coset/torsor for Aut(T). A chosen anti-map is a coordinate choice.
- Every tested anti-map reverses scores: score(sigma(v)) = n-1-score(v).
- The images of a vertex under all anti-maps are exactly the dual
  automorphism orbit, so node perspectives are swapped orbit-to-orbit.
- H=7 and H=21 remain absent in exact SC classes through n=7; unit-distance
  sees 7/21 only as decomposed edge-carrier echoes, not as tournament H.
- The n=21 Moser/exact row splits 57 = 20 spine + 37 bulk, and 37 is a
  centered-hex shell number. That is a recursive carrier signal, not an
  H=21 realization.
